# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env and .env*.local are gitignored at the
# repo root, which covers every workspace under it. Never commit real values,
# and never give a secret a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name: that prefix ships it to the
# browser in the page source.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# ui/app pulls only NEXT_PUBLIC_* out of the same file via next.config.ts
# (Next only looks in its own dir). On Vercel there is no root file, so set
# the NEXT_PUBLIC_* names in the Vercel project instead.

# ---- Privy embedded wallets (ui/app) ------------------------------------------
# The app id is public: it only names the app to Privy. Blank: the app runs signed out, for practice money.
# Each player gets an embedded Solana wallet: Solana has to be on in the dashboard's embedded wallets.
# Ours is cmuzqwmig01200dl8gf8j8tf2. The app's origin has to be in the Privy dashboard's
# allowed origins first (http://localhost:3101 for local work); docs/PRIVY-SETUP.md.
# Privy's app secret is not needed by anything in the repo: keep it out of this file.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=

# ---- Sentry (ui/app) -------------------------------------------------------------
# Errors, traces and a replay of the minute before each error (ui/app/src/lib/sentry.ts).
# The DSN only lets a browser send events, so it may be public. Blank: Sentry is off.
# Off in `next dev` too, unless NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DEV=1.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DEV=1
# Uploads source maps at build, so stacks read as our source. Build-time only, a secret:
# set it in the Vercel project (Sentry > Settings > Auth Tokens), never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ---- Analytics (ui/app): PostHog ------------------------------------------------
# The project's key from PostHog → Settings → Project: public by design, it only writes events.
# Blank: no analytics at all. Events go through /ingest on the app's own domain (next.config.ts).
# What is sent, and why each event, is in ui/app/src/lib/analytics.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# us or eu, whichever the project was made in. Blank: us.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_REGION=
# 1 to send from `bun run dev` too. Blank: only production builds send, so a laptop never spends the free plan.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_DEV=

# ---- Landing (ui/landing, server-only) ----------------------------------------
# The Apps Script endpoint the waitlist posts to. An open write endpoint, so it
# stays server side: never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
WAITLIST_SHEET_URL=

# ---- Network: Solana (everything) -------------------------------------------------
# devnet, mainnet-beta or localnet; blank is devnet. The one switch: it picks the cluster, Circle's
# USDC and the public RPC for the relayer, the deploy script and the apps. Each finds the game in
# packages/contracts/deployments/solana-<cluster>.json, written by `bun run deploy:solana`.
# The web app takes it too (next.config.ts), for its explorer links and labels before the relayer
# has spoken; on Vercel, where there is no root file, NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_CLUSTER. Blank: devnet.
SKECH_SOLANA_CLUSTER=devnet
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_CLUSTER=
# The deploy's keypair file: the program's upgrade authority and the game's first admin.
# SOLANA_DEPLOYER_KEYPAIR=~/.config/solana/id.json
# Who owns the treasury's USDC account, where collected fees land. Blank: the deployer. On mainnet, the
# relayer's address: fees land in its own USDC account, and its gas keeper buys its SOL back with them.
# SOLANA_TREASURY=
# A private RPC per cluster (Helius, Triton): the public ones rate-limit, and on mainnet a staked
# RPC (SWQoS) is what lands placements inside the 3-second window. Blank: the public RPC.
# Its URL carries its token: server-only, never a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name.
SOLANA_DEVNET_RPC_URL=
SOLANA_MAINNET_BETA_RPC_URL=
# Their websockets, when not the RPC with ws:// (the deploy script confirms over it).
# SOLANA_DEVNET_WS_URL=
# SOLANA_MAINNET_BETA_WS_URL=

# ---- Relayer (packages/relayer, server-only) -----------------------------------
# The relayer's keypair: it pays every fee and rent and signs as the oracle. A file locally, or its 64
# bytes as JSON ([12,34,...]) on the box, where infra/deploy.sh --env ships it. Keep SOL in it.
# Blank both, and `bun run dev` leaves the relayer out (on localnet it uses ~/.config/solana/id.json).
SOLANA_RELAYER_KEYPAIR=
SOLANA_RELAYER_SECRET_KEY=
# Requests a second the relayer asks of its RPC, all told: sends first, then confirmations, the
# blockhash, players' reads and the sweep last. Under the plan's limit (mainnet bills each). Blank: 15.
# SOLANA_RPC_RPS=
# Priority fee, micro-lamports per compute unit: fixed, or blank for what recent blocks paid to write
# the pool, capped at the max (50,000 off mainnet, 2,000,000 on it).
# SOLANA_PRIORITY_MICROLAMPORTS=
# SOLANA_PRIORITY_MAX_MICROLAMPORTS=
# The least one piece may stake, USDC millionths, told to the apps. Blank: 10000 (1¢), so a single dot goes in.
# A 1¢ piece's 1% fee does not pay its gas (about $0.0008): the apps gather a line into 10¢ pieces, and pieces
# under 10¢ are limited to 10 at once and 2 a second for each player (src/limits.ts).
# SOLANA_MIN_PIECE_STAKE=
# RELAYER_SOLANA_PORT=3104
# Where it listens. Blank: 127.0.0.1, this machine only, which is right behind Caddy on the box and
# for `bun run dev`. 0.0.0.0 to be reached from elsewhere, e.g. a phone on the same network.
# RELAYER_HOST=
# The engine's signing address (the address of ENGINE_PRIVATE_KEY). Set, the relayer listens only to an engine
# that signs as it: nothing else's prices are vouched for, or its bars settled on. Blank: whichever engine
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENGINE_URL reaches. infra/deploy.sh --env ships it.
RELAYER_ENGINE_SIGNER=
# Where the relayer keeps its state file (bets not yet settled). Blank: packages/relayer. The box: /var/lib/skech-relayer.
# RELAYER_STATE_DIR=
# The paths library the pricer reads. Blank: packages/core/src/dots-lib.bin.
# SKECH_LIB=
# The relayer's Sentry project (packages/relayer/src/sentry.ts): crashes, and pieces not placed, seconds
# not settled, the sweep, the state file and low SOL, at most once an hour each. Blank: off. Only under
# systemd on the box, unless RELAYER_SENTRY_DEV=1. infra/deploy.sh --env ships it.
RELAYER_SENTRY_DSN=
# RELAYER_SENTRY_DEV=1
# The gas keeper (packages/relayer/src/solana/keeper.ts): every KEEPER_EVERY_MS it reads the relayer's SOL
# and USDC. Under the floor, it buys SOL back to the target with USDC through Jupiter; over the cap, it sends
# what is above the keep to the cold wallet. Off unless KEEPER_ENABLED=1; off mainnet or with
# KEEPER_DRY_RUN=1 it only logs what it would do. infra/deploy.sh --env ships all of these.
# KEEPER_ENABLED=1
# KEEPER_DRY_RUN=1
# KEEPER_EVERY_MS=300000
# SOL: buy when under the floor, up to the target.
# KEEPER_SOL_FLOOR=0.1
# KEEPER_SOL_TARGET=0.3
# Jupiter's Metis swap API, and a key from developers.jup.ag/portal (sent as x-api-key). Server-only.
# KEEPER_JUPITER_URL=https://api.jup.ag/swap/v1
# KEEPER_JUPITER_API_KEY=
# KEEPER_SLIPPAGE_BPS=50
# One swap this often at most, at most this much USDC swapped a UTC day, never into the reserve.
# KEEPER_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=3600000
# KEEPER_DAILY_CAP_USDC=30
# KEEPER_USDC_RESERVE=0
# A wallet the relayer sends USDC to once it holds over the cap, keeping the keep: at most the max at once,
# once an hour. Blank: nothing is sent anywhere.
# KEEPER_COLD_WALLET=
# KEEPER_USDC_CAP=100
# KEEPER_USDC_KEEP=20
# KEEPER_COLD_MAX_USDC=1000
# Where the web app reaches the relayer. `bun run dev` runs it at ws://localhost:3104/ws.
# Built into the page at build time: on Vercel set it for Production (and Preview), then redeploy.
# The box: wss://api.skech.trade/solana/ws
NEXT_PUBLIC_RELAYER_URL=


# ---- Engine (packages/engine, server-only) -------------------------------------
# The wallet that signs quotes. Blank: the engine will not start, except under `bun run dev:engine`
# (--dev), which signs with a throwaway wallet each run.
ENGINE_PRIVATE_KEY=
# It signs under one fixed EIP-712 domain (packages/engine/src/quote.rs): nothing to set.
# How close two venues must be to agree on a price, in basis points: Coinbase's is signed if Binance or
# Kraken is this close, else theirs if they are this close to each other, else nothing. Blank: 15 (0.15%).
ENGINE_BAND_BPS=
# Where it listens. Blank: 127.0.0.1. 0.0.0.0 to reach a laptop's engine from a phone.
# ENGINE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ENGINE_PORT=3102
# Players connected at once (the relayer has slots of its own). Blank: 500.
# ENGINE_MAX_CLIENTS=500
# Sentry: a panic, with its stack, before the engine goes down. Sent only where SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT
# is set (the box's unit sets production), or with ENGINE_SENTRY_DEV=1.
ENGINE_SENTRY_DSN=
# ENGINE_SENTRY_DEV=1
# Where the app reaches the engine. Blank: ws://localhost:3102/ws, which is right only for `bun run dev`.
# Built into the page at build time: on Vercel set it for Production (and Preview), then redeploy.
# The box: wss://api.skech.trade/engine/ws
NEXT_PUBLIC_ENGINE_URL=

# ---- Social: profiles, follows, the leaderboard, the live feed (packages/relayer/src/social) ----
# A worker in the relayer, on 127.0.0.1:SOCIAL_PORT, behind Caddy's /social/*. Server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Postgres: in Supabase, Connect > Session pooler (port 5432), with ?sslmode=require (docs/SETUP.md).
# Blank: no social service; the game is not affected either way.
SOCIAL_DATABASE_URL=
# The app's web origins, comma-separated: a page from any other is refused. Production and preview domains.
SOCIAL_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3101,http://127.0.0.1:3101
# SOCIAL_PORT=3105
# Where it listens. Blank: 127.0.0.1, behind Caddy. 0.0.0.0 to reach a laptop's from a phone on the same network.
# SOCIAL_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Requests a second it may make of the relayer's RPC, reading the game's history: on top of SOLANA_RPC_RPS,
# so keep the two under the RPC plan's limit. Blank: 2.
# SOCIAL_RPC_RPS=2
# How far back it reads the game's history on its first start. Blank: 30 days.
# SOCIAL_BACKFILL_DAYS=30
# Where the web app reaches it. Blank: /social on the relayer's host (https://api.skech.trade/social), or
# http://localhost:3105 with a relayer on this machine. Built into the page at build time.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_URL=
